{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"ebd3c908b8ff60de","name":"card_event_prolonged_siege","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Finland/events/card_event_prolonged_siege","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"PROLONGED SIEGE","text":"Draw 4 cards. Discard them at the end of your next turn.","flavorText":"During WWII, Finland participated in the Siege of Leningrad (now St. Petersburg) as part of its alliance with Germany during the Continuation War (1941–1944). At the time Finland fought to regain territories lost to the Soviet Union after the Winter War (1939–1940), including the Karelian Isthmus and the city of Viipuri (Vyborg). In 1941, Finnish forces advanced to the pre-1940 Soviet-Finnish border north of Leningrad, cutting off land routes and contributing to the blockade of the city. However, Finland halted its advance at the historic border, refusing to push further into Soviet territory or directly bombard Leningrad. This decision stemmed from political caution and a focus on defensive goals rather than total warfare. While Finnish troops blockaded Leningrad’s northern approaches, they avoided active direct participation in the brutal urban siege conducted by the German forces. The Finnish front remained static until 1944, when Soviet breakthroughs in the Vyborg–Petrozavodsk Offensive forced Finland to retreat and eventually negotiate an armistice with the Soviet Union.","faction":"Finland","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_prolonged_siege","title":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_prolonged_siege_title","SourceString":"PROLONGED SIEGE","LocalizedString":"PROLONGED SIEGE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Finland","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_prolonged_siege_text","SourceString":"Draw 4 cards. Discard them at the end of your next turn.","LocalizedString":"Draw 4 cards. Discard them at the end of your next turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_prolonged_siege_history","SourceString":"During WWII, Finland participated in the Siege of Leningrad (now St. Petersburg) as part of its alliance with Germany during the Continuation War (1941–1944). At the time Finland fought to regain territories lost to the Soviet Union after the Winter War (1939–1940), including the Karelian Isthmus and the city of Viipuri (Vyborg). In 1941, Finnish forces advanced to the pre-1940 Soviet-Finnish border north of Leningrad, cutting off land routes and contributing to the blockade of the city. However, Finland halted its advance at the historic border, refusing to push further into Soviet territory or directly bombard Leningrad. This decision stemmed from political caution and a focus on defensive goals rather than total warfare. While Finnish troops blockaded Leningrad’s northern approaches, they avoided active direct participation in the brutal urban siege conducted by the German forces. The Finnish front remained static until 1944, when Soviet breakthroughs in the Vyborg–Petrozavodsk Offensive forced Finland to retreat and eventually negotiate an armistice with the Soviet Union.","LocalizedString":"During WWII, Finland participated in the Siege of Leningrad (now St. Petersburg) as part of its alliance with Germany during the Continuation War (1941–1944). At the time Finland fought to regain territories lost to the Soviet Union after the Winter War (1939–1940), including the Karelian Isthmus and the city of Viipuri (Vyborg). In 1941, Finnish forces advanced to the pre-1940 Soviet-Finnish border north of Leningrad, cutting off land routes and contributing to the blockade of the city. However, Finland halted its advance at the historic border, refusing to push further into Soviet territory or directly bombard Leningrad. This decision stemmed from political caution and a focus on defensive goals rather than total warfare. While Finnish troops blockaded Leningrad’s northern approaches, they avoided active direct participation in the brutal urban siege conducted by the German forces. The Finnish front remained static until 1944, when Soviet breakthroughs in the Vyborg–Petrozavodsk Offensive forced Finland to retreat and eventually negotiate an armistice with the Soviet Union."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardReset"],"draftBaseWeight":0.9,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Finland/Mini_Ally_Expansion_25/t_prolonged_siege.t_prolonged_siege","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Volmi Games","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/PROLONGED_SIEGE.PROLONGED_SIEGE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":368.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_prolonged_siege_photo","SourceString":"Finnish Troops and Swedish Volunteers fighting in the Russian town of Reboly, 1942.","LocalizedString":"Finnish Troops and Swedish Volunteers fighting in the Russian town of Reboly, 1942."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_prolonged_siege","owner":"card_event_prolonged_siege_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"K2Node_Event_cardReset","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_resetCardID","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_R